And it's just absurd
that, you know,

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:50.809
when it comes to like
if you kill someone

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:52.744
on accident versus purposely,

00:26:52.744 --> 00:26:54.279
there's different designations

00:26:54.279 --> 00:26:56.448
for that in our criminal code,

00:26:56.448 --> 00:26:59.050
jokes are a little
less consequential
than someone's life.

00:26:59.050 --> 00:27:01.886 align:start size:84% position:16%
So why are we
treating it like this?

00:27:01.886 --> 00:27:03.521
I don't think anyone can
actually feel that way.

00:27:03.521 --> 00:27:04.756
Of course it matters.

00:27:04.756 --> 00:27:07.158 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, when I was
losing my hair,

00:27:07.158 --> 00:27:08.860
I made jokes about
it all the time.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.695
I mean, Greg even made a joke

00:27:10.695 --> 00:27:12.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I looked like Tanner
from "Bad News Bears"

00:27:12.697 --> 00:27:14.065 align:start size:84% position:16%
without my extensions
in, I laughed.

00:27:14.065 --> 00:27:16.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought that was great.
It was funny,

00:27:16.234 --> 00:27:18.336 align:start size:84% position:16%
I had an ex-boyfriend
who was abusive

00:27:18.336 --> 00:27:19.838
and would tell me
like, you know,

00:27:19.838 --> 00:27:21.873 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Fuck you, you
rapidly aging idiot."

00:27:21.873 --> 00:27:24.743
Like how those things
are, they're different.

00:27:24.743 --> 00:27:27.145
Someone was trying to make
me feel bad about myself

00:27:27.145 --> 00:27:29.347
so he could continue to
maintain control over me.

00:27:29.347 --> 00:27:31.416 align:start size:88% position:13%
How is that not
different than somebody

00:27:31.416 --> 00:27:33.385
who is just trying
to make me laugh?

00:27:33.385 --> 00:27:34.219
Of course it is.

00:27:34.219 --> 00:27:36.254
And it's just insane.

00:27:36.254 --> 00:27:38.657
I mean all the jokes, the
times that I've gotten,

00:27:38.657 --> 00:27:42.327 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean I've been involved
in a few different scandals,

00:27:42.327 --> 00:27:45.930 align:start size:97% position:3%
one with Kimmel over jokes,
that was by accident.

00:27:45.930 --> 00:27:47.265 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was talking about
something else

00:27:47.265 --> 00:27:49.300 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I accidentally said
something offensive

00:27:49.300 --> 00:27:50.602
and I didn't mean
to be offensive,

00:27:50.602 --> 00:27:52.871
but I was treated as
if I did it on purpose.

00:27:52.871 --> 00:27:55.740
And not only is that not fair
to people making the joke,

00:27:55.740 --> 00:28:00.679 align:start size:97% position:3%
that really doesn't reserve
the absolute shaming

00:28:01.846 --> 00:28:03.081
that we should be
doing of people

00:28:03.081 --> 00:28:04.849 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are trying to
be jerks on purpose.

00:28:04.849 --> 00:28:06.718
- Right, well also with
a guy like Jimmy Kimmel

00:28:06.718 --> 00:28:09.921 align:start size:97% position:3%
who's been in blackface
multiple times and you know,

00:28:09.921 --> 00:28:12.824
making fun of the "black
accent" from Carl Malone.

00:28:12.824 --> 00:28:15.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's like that's why he's
going after someone like you

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:17.195
for a joke because
he has to, you know,

00:28:17.195 --> 00:28:20.365 align:start size:97% position:3%
bow to them forever, otherwise
they'll take him out.

00:28:20.365 --> 00:28:22.667
- Well, I sent him a book,

00:28:22.667 --> 00:28:24.836 align:start size:97% position:3%
probably the most embarrassing
thing that happened to me

00:28:24.836 --> 00:28:26.838
on air was when I made a joke

00:28:26.838 --> 00:28:29.874
about how hard it
is to give my cat

00:28:29.874 --> 00:28:33.511 align:start size:84% position:16%
a feral cat medication
versus a human.

00:28:33.511 --> 00:28:34.446
And it was during a segment

00:28:34.446 --> 00:28:36.581
about how, what his hiatus was,

00:28:36.581 --> 00:28:38.116
but we were actually also live

00:28:38.116 --> 00:28:40.185
and I think this is the last
time we were live actually.

00:28:40.185 --> 00:28:43.188
'Cause I was talking about
how it's super difficult

00:28:43.188 --> 00:28:44.923
and like the cat can
claw you or whatever.

00:28:44.923 --> 00:28:46.391
And then Greg was like,

00:28:46.391 --> 00:28:48.693
"Oh Kat, Jimmy Kimmel's son
has like a heart issue."

00:28:48.693 --> 00:28:51.329
And I like didn't realize that.

00:28:52.964 --> 00:28:55.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, I get the
Fallon and Kimmel confused

00:28:55.100 --> 00:28:57.268
and I'm now, I was like,
oh wait, I do remember.

00:28:57.268 --> 00:28:58.436
But I remember in the
article it was like

00:28:58.436 --> 00:28:59.671
my whole family's healthy.

00:28:59.671 --> 00:29:00.872 align:start size:88% position:13%
I remember before I made
the joke it was like,

00:29:00.872 --> 00:29:02.173
just so I'm not gonna get in,

00:29:02.173 --> 00:29:04.042
I was like, I'm not
gonna get in trouble.

00:29:04.042 --> 00:29:07.078
But also so much of comedy
is like swinging and missing.

00:29:07.078 --> 00:29:08.313
You know, you don't really know

00:29:08.313 --> 00:29:10.448
if something's gonna
land until you try it.

00:29:10.448 --> 00:29:13.585
And I was just doing
that and you can't make

00:29:13.585 --> 00:29:15.120
people too afraid to try

00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:17.589
or else we're gonna miss out
on some really great jokes.

00:29:17.589 --> 00:29:18.723
Not just in terms of laughter,

00:29:18.723 --> 00:29:20.592
but some of the darker subjects

00:29:20.592 --> 00:29:22.761 align:start size:84% position:16%
that can have those
healing powers.

00:29:22.761 --> 00:29:25.330
But I apologized because
I genuinely did feel bad.

00:29:25.330 --> 00:29:26.664
I was like, I didn't
mean it like that.

00:29:26.664 --> 00:29:28.366
I don't want anybody to,
you know, think I did.

00:29:28.366 --> 00:29:30.668
Everyone who watched the show

00:29:30.668 --> 00:29:32.871
was actually telling
me like, you were fine.

00:29:32.871 --> 00:29:35.273
Like, because I was holding
back tears the entire time.

00:29:35.273 --> 00:29:36.574
I felt so awful.

00:29:36.574 --> 00:29:38.109
The next day somebody posted

00:29:38.109 --> 00:29:39.944
a little tiny clip
of it on Twitter

00:29:39.944 --> 00:29:42.781 align:start size:88% position:13%
and said that I had
been making fun of him,

00:29:42.781 --> 00:29:45.550
his family because his
son had a heart problem

00:29:45.550 --> 00:29:48.119 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that it was harder to have
a cat with a heart problem

00:29:48.119 --> 00:29:49.420
than a child with
a heart problem

00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:52.624 align:start size:84% position:16%
and different,
like media outlets,

00:29:52.624 --> 00:29:53.925 align:start size:84% position:16%
like Raw Story if
you can call it that,

00:29:53.925 --> 00:29:55.193
took it and ran with it.

00:29:55.193 --> 00:29:57.428 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I was ironically
at the vet with my cat

00:29:57.428 --> 00:29:58.963
and I was like my ...

00:29:58.963 --> 00:30:00.231
Blowing up on social media,

00:30:00.231 --> 00:30:01.733
people telling me
like, "Fuck you",

00:30:01.733 --> 00:30:03.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jimmy Kimmel's sister told
me to fuck off and die.

00:30:03.935 --> 00:30:05.370
All of this stuff.

00:30:05.370 --> 00:30:08.573 align:start position:0%
And like if I had actually
said, it's actually no big deal,

00:30:08.573 --> 00:30:10.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
"fuck your kid with
a heart problem

00:30:10.141 --> 00:30:12.944 align:start position:0%
because he has a heart problem",
I would've deserved that.

00:30:12.944 --> 00:30:15.513
But I was trying to make
a funny joke about that

00:30:15.513 --> 00:30:17.382
and also about people

00:30:17.382 --> 00:30:19.284
who don't have children like me,

00:30:19.284 --> 00:30:22.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
sometimes like having a child
can be a catch-all excuse

00:30:22.187 --> 00:30:23.755
for everything and if
you don't have kid,

00:30:23.755 --> 00:30:25.256 align:start size:88% position:13%
like something that's
relatable to cat owners,

00:30:25.256 --> 00:30:26.191
something that's
relatable to people

00:30:26.191 --> 00:30:27.425
that don't have children.

00:30:27.425 --> 00:30:28.927
That's what I was trying to do.

00:30:28.927 --> 00:30:31.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't think I should
be treated the same way

00:30:31.696 --> 00:30:33.998
as if I was trying to do that.

00:30:33.998 --> 00:30:38.069
Which is a totally, I mean
that's just abhorrent, right?

00:30:38.069 --> 00:30:40.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it's, that
wasn't my intention.

00:30:40.004 --> 00:30:42.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
And again, if we make
people too afraid to try,

00:30:43.675 --> 00:30:46.277
then we're gonna lose
out on so much healing

00:30:46.277 --> 00:30:48.746
within ourselves and
also with one another

00:30:48.746 --> 00:30:50.782
through shared experiences.

00:30:50.782 --> 00:30:53.618 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I often quote Oscar Wilde
or at least loosely quote him.

00:30:53.618 --> 00:30:55.186
I mean, if you wanna
tell people the truth,

00:30:55.186 --> 00:30:56.888
you better be funny or they're
gonna punch you in the face.

00:30:56.888 --> 00:30:58.623
So it's something like that.

00:30:58.623 --> 00:30:59.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let me ask you a
couple other things,

00:30:59.724 --> 00:31:01.659
just kind of world related stuff

00:31:01.659 --> 00:31:03.494
as people can see out
your window there.

00:31:03.494 --> 00:31:05.396 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think you're at
the Fox News offices.

00:31:05.396 --> 00:31:06.531
- Yeah.

00:31:06.531 --> 00:31:08.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You are in midtown,
New York City.

00:31:08.867 --> 00:31:10.401
A city that I once lived in

00:31:10.401 --> 00:31:12.537
and loved for 20
years of my life.

00:31:12.537 --> 00:31:14.072
But every time I go back there,

00:31:14.072 --> 00:31:16.207
which is pretty much only to
do "Gutfeld!" at this point,

00:31:16.207 --> 00:31:18.142
I find it to be a
zombie of a city.

00:31:18.142 --> 00:31:20.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not the same New York
Midtown where you are.

00:31:20.378 --> 00:31:21.946 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's no business
people anymore.

00:31:21.946 --> 00:31:23.848
Everyone kind of wearing a hood,

00:31:23.848 --> 00:31:26.017
looks like they're going
to get weed or sell weed

00:31:26.017 --> 00:31:28.219
or steal weed or something.

00:31:28.219 --> 00:31:30.488 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like what is going
on in New York?

00:31:31.656 --> 00:31:33.591 align:start size:84% position:16%
- See, I wouldn't even
mind it being seedy

00:31:33.591 --> 00:31:35.793
if it was less expensive.

00:31:35.793 --> 00:31:38.429
(Rubin laughing)

00:31:38.429 --> 00:31:42.400
- A lot of things that made
New York so special too,

00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:44.135
like the little
small businesses,

00:31:44.135 --> 00:31:45.937 align:start size:97% position:3%
immigrant owned restaurants,
those, you know,

00:31:45.937 --> 00:31:48.706
special little gems,
a lot of them are gone

00:31:48.706 --> 00:31:53.211
because they couldn't survive
being illegal in the pandemic

00:31:53.211 --> 00:31:55.980
and everything is so expensive.

00:31:55.980 --> 00:31:57.582
I mean it's, it's so crazy.

00:31:57.582 --> 00:31:59.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean I've been thinking
about maybe having

00:31:59.017 --> 00:32:01.185
one of those baby things
myself with my husband,

00:32:01.185 --> 00:32:03.288 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we're like, where
would we put it?

00:32:03.288 --> 00:32:04.923
- You know, we have no taxes,

00:32:04.923 --> 00:32:08.860 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have no taxes on baby
related stuff here in Florida.

00:32:08.860 --> 00:32:11.963 align:start size:97% position:3%
Florida, I say it to you
every time I see you, Florida.

00:32:11.963 --> 00:32:15.033
- I'm just, I know and I
would, it's just this job.

00:32:15.033 --> 00:32:19.470
I am like less concerned with
being mugged on the street

00:32:19.470 --> 00:32:23.041
than I am knowing for
a fact I'm being gonna,

00:32:23.041 --> 00:32:25.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, I am being
mugged by the government.

00:32:25.276 --> 00:32:27.211
They take so much of my income

00:32:27.211 --> 00:32:31.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I walk outside and I'm
like, what is this for?

00:32:31.649 --> 00:32:33.618 align:start size:81% position:19%
Where did you,
you stole my money

00:32:33.618 --> 00:32:36.054
and then what did
you spend it on?

00:32:36.054 --> 00:32:40.458
And it's so expensive to live
here, it's just ridiculous.

00:32:40.458 --> 00:32:42.327
- I mean, do you
find anyone there

00:32:42.327 --> 00:32:43.828
that thinks that
it's going well?

00:32:43.828 --> 00:32:46.597
I mean, I still, I know a few
remaining people in New York

00:32:46.597 --> 00:32:48.132
and everyone, I kid you not,

00:32:48.132 --> 00:32:49.901
I think literally
everyone right now

00:32:49.901 --> 00:32:51.502
is in the process of leaving.

00:32:51.502 --> 00:32:53.771
And I already know
probably 20 people

00:32:53.771 --> 00:32:56.107
that left in the
last three years.

00:32:56.107 --> 00:32:58.042
- We would, I mean, my
husband's from New York.

00:32:58.042 --> 00:33:00.878 align:start size:88% position:13%
My life dream was always
to live in New York.

00:33:00.878 --> 00:33:02.880
I mean, at this point it's just,

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:04.782
I mean I'm also, you know, I'm,

00:33:04.782 --> 00:33:05.984
I've grown up a little bit.

00:33:05.984 --> 00:33:07.251
I'm, you know, married,

00:33:07.251 --> 00:33:08.853
I'm not really going out a lot

00:33:10.221 --> 00:33:12.323 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I'm just sit, you
know, I'm at working a lot,

00:33:12.323 --> 00:33:14.826
so I'm at home a
lot and it's just

00:33:14.826 --> 00:33:16.861
like my home's not that big.

00:33:17.996 --> 00:33:19.897
When I say home, I
mean handful of rooms

00:33:19.897 --> 00:33:21.866
that I'm paying
so much money for

00:33:21.866 --> 00:33:23.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I don't even
own, I'm just renting.

00:33:23.601 --> 00:33:25.169
And I, yeah, I don't know.

00:33:25.169 --> 00:33:26.504
I mean I feel like also

00:33:26.504 --> 00:33:28.806 align:start size:88% position:13%
a lot of this
commercial real estate,

00:33:28.806 --> 00:33:30.575
I mean a lot of people
are working from home.

00:33:30.575 --> 00:33:33.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
A lot of the, you
know, the government,

00:33:33.678 --> 00:33:35.079
the state government
here, city government,

00:33:35.079 --> 00:33:36.180
it's funded on this stuff.

00:33:36.180 --> 00:33:37.815
And when that goes away,

00:33:37.815 --> 00:33:40.451 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean you pointed it out
too, all the for lease signs.

00:33:40.451 --> 00:33:41.786
A lot of people aren't like,

00:33:41.786 --> 00:33:43.921
I wanna take on this
really expensive lease

00:33:43.921 --> 00:33:48.126
in this place that's sort of
look like it's collapsing.

00:33:48.126 --> 00:33:50.128
So I think it's gonna
get worse actually.

00:33:50.128 --> 00:33:51.629
- Yeah, you know, it's funny,

00:33:51.629 --> 00:33:53.798
you must know Douglas Murray
who's a Fox News contributor.

00:33:53.798 --> 00:33:55.233
- Yes.

00:33:55.233 --> 00:33:57.168 align:start position:0%
- So last time I did "Gutfeld!"
and I saw you at the show,

00:33:57.168 --> 00:33:59.570
I went out to dinner
with Douglas after,

00:33:59.570 --> 00:34:02.373 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he's in from London now,
living in New York City.

00:34:02.373 --> 00:34:04.642
And he kept telling me
how magical it was there

00:34:04.642 --> 00:34:06.844
and I kept thinking,
man, if you only knew

00:34:06.844 --> 00:34:08.379
what it used to be like,

00:34:08.379 --> 00:34:11.649
but you are seeing the
vestiges of magical.

00:34:11.649 --> 00:34:13.184 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I guess that
could still be magical

00:34:13.184 --> 00:34:15.053
if you're from somewhere else.

00:34:15.053 --> 00:34:17.321
- Yeah, I love Douglas Murray.

00:34:17.321 --> 00:34:18.523
We sat next to each other

00:34:18.523 --> 00:34:19.824 align:start size:84% position:16%
at the White House
Correspondents dinner.

00:34:19.824 --> 00:34:21.626
- He is a, he is a good one.

00:34:23.094 --> 00:34:24.328
What else is on your mind
politically at the moment?

00:34:24.328 --> 00:34:26.364
I mean, obviously we
can do the woke stuff

00:34:26.364 --> 00:34:27.799
till we're like
blue in the face,

00:34:27.799 --> 00:34:29.801 align:start size:81% position:19%
but what about
the sort of divide

00:34:29.801 --> 00:34:31.502 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's now happening between
the red and the blue?

00:34:31.502 --> 00:34:33.771 align:start size:88% position:13%
I assume as a
libertarian you're cool

00:34:33.771 --> 00:34:36.074 align:start size:84% position:16%
with this resurgence
of federalism.

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:42.113
- Right, I mean okay,
as I mentioned before,

00:34:42.113 --> 00:34:46.651 align:start size:97% position:3%
talking about feelings I think
is actually a good thing.

00:34:46.651 --> 00:34:49.921
I know that a lot of the refrain

00:34:49.921 --> 00:34:52.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it comes to
people on the right,

00:34:52.156 --> 00:34:53.958
I mean you included,
is that, you know,

00:34:53.958 --> 00:34:55.126 align:start size:84% position:16%
facts don't care
about your feelings.

00:34:55.126 --> 00:34:57.195
And I totally get that.

00:34:57.195 --> 00:34:59.163 align:start size:81% position:19%
But it's also true
that sometimes

00:34:59.163 --> 00:35:01.399
feelings don't care
about your facts.

00:35:01.399 --> 00:35:04.168
And I know that it's
the only explanation

00:35:04.168 --> 00:35:07.004
for every relationship
I had in my twenties

00:35:07.004 --> 00:35:10.575
where I was like, but
I, but I love him.

00:35:10.575 --> 00:35:12.076 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're like, he
treats you horrible,

00:35:12.076 --> 00:35:14.112
he has no job, he's mean to
you, he's cheating on you.

00:35:14.112 --> 00:35:15.746
I was like, but I love him.

00:35:15.746 --> 00:35:18.382
So like humans are
emotional creatures.

00:35:18.382 --> 00:35:19.750
We are gonna have emotions.

00:35:19.750 --> 00:35:21.219 align:start size:84% position:16%
And as someone who's
pro-free speech,

00:35:21.219 --> 00:35:23.321
I think that includes
speech about feelings.

00:35:23.321 --> 00:35:24.956
So I think that that's something

00:35:24.956 --> 00:35:26.691 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the right should
acknowledge more and again,

00:35:26.691 --> 00:35:28.226 align:start size:84% position:16%
bring up that
distinction between

00:35:28.226 --> 00:35:29.660 align:start size:81% position:19%
why you're sharing
your feelings.

00:35:29.660 --> 00:35:31.195 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's a difference between
sharing your feelings

00:35:31.195 --> 00:35:33.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
to try to express
yourself to another person

